  "notes": "Drawn from one right-side photo of 747-400F B-2423 (January 2025); the aft fuselage's streaks are simplified. Right-side photo only; the left side is assumed to mirror it. The narrowbodies (737/757) wear a simpler version. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on B-2423: the Chinese name sits a small gap under AIRLINES (it had been drawn touching it) and is lettered lighter and spaced out; lengths agree. This is the 747-400F, not SF's commonest type (the 757-200F, then 767-300F and 737F); a redraw on the 757 from its own photos is the larger job left.",
